## Reproduction and target-clearance assertions

**Divisor-one reproduction: PASS, BIT_IDENTICAL.** With the diagnostic provisioning divisor and its corresponding clearance factor set to one, and the quantile-only refinement inactive, the strict dense function body matched every sealed ndarray field at boundary 0 and over all 48 boundaries for 5 receipts, 40 anchors, and 120 committed configurations. The explicit required fields—bits, transmissions, mode counts, transmitted mode counts, and maximum radiated power—were bit-identical; recorded bits, joules, and served counts also matched exactly.

That all-ones assertion proves reproduction of the original rule only; it does not prove clearance when the divisor is `q`. For the latter I ran seven independent coupled/capped fixtures through both scalar and dense paths. Every uncapped strict fixture satisfied both `SINR_nominal >= Gamma/q` and `q*SINR_nominal >= target-mode threshold`; the two fixtures unable to satisfy them were capped at 1.65 W and were allowed to remain target-infeasible. The focused control goes red on the defect: simple division leaves three no-mode transmissions in each of its two low-power coupled fixtures, while strict clearance leaves zero.

Scalar and dense results agree on all seven fixtures: maximum power is binary64-identical, no-mode counts and certificate iteration counts are identical, and bits/joules agree within the declared `2e-14` relative tolerance. Both paths reported zero uncertified strict fixture cases.

## Strict-clearance algorithm (reviewed specification)

The dense site is the private catalogue evaluator loaded unchanged from `/home/sat/mcrl-v025-ladder-ws/.scratch/ladder-floor-20260910/cleared_margin_batch.py`; the scalar site is the matching private context in `scalar_diagnostics.py`. The beam runner's selection and 48-boundary committed scores use the dense site. Its per-boundary diagnostics use the scalar site.

For each TDM slot, the inherited capped fixed-point solver first uses `Gamma/q`, its unchanged residual/relative stopping rules, the unchanged final fixed-point update, and `nextafter(final*(1+2e-9), +inf)`. The strict loop then recomputes nominal SINR from the current power vector. A row is deficient only when it is active, not forced, below the cap, and either `SINR_nominal < Gamma/q` or `q*SINR_nominal < target-mode threshold`.

If no row is deficient, the loop terminates successfully. Otherwise it recomputes required power with the same interference map, applies the same `1+2e-9` and `nextafter` numerical nudge, caps it at 1.65 W, and raises only deficient entries monotonically. Each refinement update consumes one of the original solver's remaining iterations. The total inherited budget is 65536 iterations per slot/configuration; if a deficiency remains when that budget is exhausted, the certificate becomes INVALID. Forced or capped links are not raised beyond the cap and may miss the target. No tolerance, nudge, physical constant, cap, or budget changed.

The only runner adaptation is wiring: a hash-checking read-only adapter loads those exact dense and scalar implementations and selects both sites for the strict arm. The strict dense source SHA-256 is `bf9f3cfecba54125c6a7736f550032e6bd7292f03f8fc6281f1d02979c14a85f`. The sealed `batch.py` and `architectures.py` sources match the ladder workspace byte-for-byte. On the twenty-anchor ladder panel, all 60 stored committed B/U/J profiles replayed bit-identically (zero relative difference), and the pooled strict gap remained +0.512537182%.

## Held-fixed execution contract

Each width uses `V025_PROBE_R2/world/1` and `/2`, steps 0–3, 100 users, the same world tapes and seeds, neutral nearest-eligible baseline, exact binary64 `F = B - eta_ref E` with `eta_ref = 19,720,681.00172232 bit/J`, deterministic cyclic exact best response until a full pass has no strictly improving legal move, and the same service guard. Every strict anchor's terminal unilateral certificate is true.

The joint catalogue uses the same bounded catalogue: same-beam subsets of size 2–4 with the 1,024-generation cap, victim plus top-2/top-3 physical contributors, complete-beam evacuations, and the 4,096 global cap. Selection uses realised boundary 0; only after selection are B/U/J committed over all 48 realised boundaries and pooled. The two seeds remain `3525272352645343090` and `3445540383109071487`. The source tree is the same sealed tree used by the ladder implementation.

