+        "",
+        "For each realised boundary and TDM slot, C2 chooses OFF or a non-dominated DVB-S2 ACM mode for every transmitting beam. A link decoded by C1 may only retain or increase its credited mode; a failed C1 transmission may be switched off or assigned any frontier mode. This pointwise non-regression makes every C1-served user's integrated bits nondecreasing, so the unchanged service guard and rate target cannot regress; the reported endpoint counts verify that invariant.",
+        "",
+        "For a discrete target vector, the inner solve is direct: `p = (I - diag(gamma/g) C)^-1 diag(gamma/g) n`, using the exact realised direct gains and full masked co-channel cross-gain matrix. Solutions are rejected if non-positive, singular, above the unchanged 1.65 W per-beam cap, outside a `5e-10 W` equation residual, or below their unchanged ACM threshold by more than binary64 tolerance. PA, active-chain, and active-satellite power are then evaluated with the unchanged energy model.",
