+        f"Detailed receipt: `{receipt_path.relative_to(REPO)}` — SHA-256 `{sha256(receipt_path)}`. Script SHA-256: `{sha256(Path(__file__).resolve())}`.",
+        "",
+        "The run is single-process (`max_workers=1`) and the command pins each numerical library to one thread.",
+        "",
+        "## What was and was not reached",
+        "",
+        "Reached: eight real anchors under both provisioning rules; the actual committed fixed assignment for each pair; independent C1 replay; per-anchor and pooled efficiency, served and target counts; exact realised interference in every visited C2 mode vector; unchanged cap/guard/target; exact additive regime decomposition; and an evidence-based implementability classification.",
+        "",
+        "Not reached: no globally certified discrete-mode optimum, relaxation bound, exhaustive mode-table enumeration, test-split or population inference, uncertainty interval, causal online controller, learned controller, or proof that the reported best-known values are ceilings. The two rules fix different pipeline-committed assignments, so their absolute efficiencies are not a same-assignment causal contrast between provisioning rules. This diagnostic supplies feasible lower bounds on control-law headroom only.",
